---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/paths";

const contact = (await getEntry("contact", "contact"))!.data;
const email = contact.enquiry_email || contact.email;
const updated = "9 October 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that apply when you use this site or buy a GrintByte product."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-grint mt-8 space-y-8 text-base leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Welcome to GrintByte ("we", "us", or "our"). By accessing our website, purchasing our
        software licenses, or downloading our digital products, you agree to be bound by these
        Terms of Service.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">1. Nature of the products</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          GrintByte is a digital software studio providing pre-built software, extensions, digital
          plugins and software components. We offer digital licenses for off-the-shelf software
          products delivered electronically.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">2. Merchant of Record (Lemon Squeezy)</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Our order processing, payment settlement and tax compliance are facilitated by our
          Merchant of Record, Lemon Squeezy (Lemon Squeezy, LLC). When you purchase a license from
          GrintByte:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Lemon Squeezy is the authorized reseller and Merchant of Record for the transaction.</li>
          <li>
            Your payment details are processed under Lemon Squeezy's
            <a href="https://www.lemonsqueezy.com/terms" rel="noopener" class="text-brand underline">Terms of Service</a>
            and
            <a href="https://www.lemonsqueezy.com/privacy" rel="noopener" class="text-brand underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Invoicing, local tax calculation (VAT/GST/Sales Tax) and payment processing security
            are managed by Lemon Squeezy.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">3. Software licensing and usage</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            Our WordPress plugins, both the free and the Pro versions, are licensed under the GNU
            General Public License (GPL). You are free to use, study and modify the code on your
            own sites, as the GPL provides.
          </li>
          <li>
            What you purchase is a license key. Upon successful payment, you are granted a
            non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use that key according to the license selected
            at checkout.
          </li>
          <li>
            License keys and our delivery, update and support services are not part of the GPL
            code. You may not resell, lease, sublicense or share license keys, in whole or in part,
            unless explicitly permitted under your specific license tier.
          </li>
          <li>
            Automated product updates and official technical support remain tied strictly to a
            valid, active license key.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">4. Digital delivery</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          All software packages and license keys are delivered electronically and automatically
          upon payment confirmation. You will receive an immediate on-screen download link and an
          automated confirmation email containing your license credentials.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">5. Product updates and technical support</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            An active license grants you access to product updates and technical support for the
            duration of the license period stated at checkout.
          </li>
          <li>
            Technical support covers bug fixes, software compatibility updates and setup guidance
            for the software as provided. It does not cover bespoke engineering, unverified
            third-party plugin conflicts outside our control, or server environment
            troubleshooting.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">6. Warranty and liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Our software is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranty of any kind,
          express or implied. While we thoroughly test our products against standard platform
          releases, GrintByte does not guarantee that the software will be error-free or operate
          uninterrupted across every individual server configuration or third-party environment.
          In no event shall GrintByte be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental or
          consequential damages resulting from the use or inability to use our products. Nothing
          in this section limits the promises in our
          <a href={withBase("/refunds")} class="text-brand underline">refund policy</a> or rights
          that the law of your country grants you and does not allow to be limited.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">7. Changes to terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We reserve the right to revise these Terms of Service at any time. Any changes will be
          posted on this page with an updated modification date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">8. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          For any questions regarding these terms, please contact us at
          <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class="text-brand underline">{email}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
